    {
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Average startup time (selected range)",
      "description": "Time from launching a server to a working connection, averaged: each session starts each server once, too few samples for a percentile. Claude Code gives up after 30 s by default. The first launch downloads the server and can take a minute; run `make mcp-check` once to warm the caches. uvx (prometheus) re-resolves its package on every start, so it is slowest.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
